; Exports of the 32-bit Windows DLL. The functions are __stdcall, whose
; symbols carry the size of their arguments; J2534 applications look the
; plain names up, so the DLL is linked with --kill-at, and the import library
; is made from this file by `dlltool --kill-at` so that it maps each
; decorated symbol to its plain export.
; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
; Ordinals as Tactrix's op20pt32.dll numbers them (alphabetical, 1-14),
; for an application that imports by ordinal.
EXPORTS
    PassThruClose@4 @1
    PassThruConnect@20 @2
    PassThruDisconnect@4 @3
    PassThruGetLastError@4 @4
    PassThruIoctl@16 @5
    PassThruOpen@8 @6
    PassThruReadMsgs@16 @7
    PassThruReadVersion@16 @8
    PassThruSetProgrammingVoltage@12 @9
    PassThruStartMsgFilter@24 @10
    PassThruStartPeriodicMsg@16 @11
    PassThruStopMsgFilter@8 @12
    PassThruStopPeriodicMsg@8 @13
    PassThruWriteMsgs@16 @14
    DllRegisterServer@0 @15 PRIVATE
    DllUnregisterServer@0 @16 PRIVATE
